@startuml parser

title PGN Parser (Phase 3 complete)

class Parser {
    + Parser()
    + ~Parser()
    + loadGame(Game&, filePath : string, meta : GameMetadata*) : bool
    + saveGame(Game const&, filePath : string, meta : GameMetadata const*) : bool
    -- private helpers --
    - parseMoveToken(token : string, game : Game&, color : bool) : bool
    - applyTokens(game : Game&, tokens, pos, isVariation : bool) : void
    - moveToSAN(move : Move const&) : string
    - writeNode(os, node : GameNode*, moveNum : int&, isWhite : bool&, firstInVariation : bool) : void
}

struct GameMetadata {
    + event : string
    + site : string
    + date : string
    + round : string
    + white : string
    + black : string
    + result : string
    + whiteElo : int
    + blackElo : int
    + eco : string
    + opening : string
    + GameMetadata()
}

enum TokenType {
    TOK_MOVE_NUM
    TOK_MOVE
    TOK_LPAREN
    TOK_RPAREN
    TOK_COMMENT
    TOK_RESULT
    TOK_EOF
}

struct Token {
    + type : TokenType
    + value : string
}

class Game {
}

class GameTree {
}

class GameNode {
}

Parser ..> Game : loads into / saves from
Parser ..> GameMetadata : fills on load / reads on save
Parser ..> Token : produces (tokenizer)
Parser ..> GameTree : walks via Game::getTree()
Parser ..> GameNode : visits via writeNode()

note right of Parser
  loadGame() pipeline:
  1. Parse [Header "value"] tags → GameMetadata
  2. Tokenize move text → vector<Token>
  3. applyTokens() recursive descent:
     - TOK_LPAREN  → game.startVariation(), recurse
     - TOK_RPAREN  → return (end variation)
     - TOK_COMMENT → game.setComment()
     - TOK_RESULT  → break
     - TOK_MOVE    → parseMoveToken() → game.checkMove()
  Handles: e8=Q promotion, +/# flags,
  file/rank/square disambiguation

  saveGame() pipeline:
  1. Write [Header "value"] lines from GameMetadata
  2. writeNode() walks GameTree from root:
     - Emits move numbers (1. / 1...)
     - Emits SAN via moveToSAN()
     - Emits {comment} if present
     - Recursively emits ( variation ) branches
end note

@enduml
